{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n    else:\n        # Use a list to store the last four values: [fib(i-4), fib(i-3), fib(i-2), fib(i-1)]\n        # Initialize with base cases for n=0, 1, 2, 3\n        fib_values = [0, 0, 2, 0] # Corresponds to fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n\n        for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n            next_fib = fib_values[3] + fib_values[2] + fib_values[1] + fib_values[0]\n            # Shift values: fib(i-3), fib(i-2), fib(i-1), fib(i)\n            fib_values[0] = fib_values[1]\n            fib_values[1] = fib_values[2]\n            fib_values[2] = fib_values[3]\n            fib_values[3] = next_fib\n\n        return fib_values[3]"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "def median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # For odd number of elements, return the middle element as a float.\n        return float(sorted_l[n // 2])\n    else:\n        # For even number of elements, return the average of the two middle elements.\n        mid1 = sorted_l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_l[n // 2]\n        return (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0"}
